# CSS BASIC NOTES

## 1. What is CSS?
CSS stands for **Cascading Style Sheets**. It is used to style and design HTML webpages.

**Uses of CSS:**
- Change text color and background color.
- Set font size and font style.
- Add borders and spacing.
- Control webpage layout.
- Make websites responsive.

## 2. Types of CSS

### a) Inline CSS
CSS is written inside an HTML element using the `style` attribute.

```html
<p style="color: red;">Hello World</p>
```

### b) Internal CSS
CSS is written inside the `<style>` tag in the HTML document.

```html
<html>
<head>
<style>
p {
    color: blue;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p>Hello World</p>
</body>
</html>
```

### c) External CSS
CSS is written in a separate `.css` file and linked to the HTML file.

**HTML file:**
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
```

**style.css:**
```css
p {
    color: green;
}
```

## 3. CSS Syntax

```css
selector {
    property: value;
}
```

**Example:**
```css
h1 {
    color: red;
    font-size: 30px;
}
```

- **Selector:** Selects the HTML element.
- **Property:** Specifies what to change.
- **Value:** Specifies how it should look.

## 4. CSS Selectors

### Element Selector
Selects all elements with a particular tag name.

```css
p {
    color: blue;
}
```

### ID Selector
Selects an element with a specific ID. It uses `#`.

```css
#heading {
    color: red;
}
```

### Class Selector
Selects elements with a particular class. It uses `.`.

```css
.title {
    color: green;
}
```

### Universal Selector
Selects all HTML elements.

```css
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}
```

## 5. CSS Colors and Background

```css
body {
    background-color: lightblue;
}

h1 {
    color: red;
}
```

Colors can be specified using color names, hexadecimal values, RGB, and HSL.

```css
h1 {
    color: #ff0000;
}
```

## 6. CSS Text and Fonts

```css
p {
    color: black;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: underline;
}
```

**Important properties:**
- `color` – Changes text color.
- `font-size` – Changes text size.
- `font-family` – Changes the font.
- `font-weight` – Controls text thickness.
- `text-align` – Aligns text.
- `text-decoration` – Adds or removes text decoration.

## 7. CSS Border

The `border` property adds a border around an element.

```css
div {
    border: 2px solid black;
}
```

Other border styles include `dotted`, `dashed`, and `double`.

## 8. CSS Margin and Padding

- **Margin:** Space outside an element's border.
- **Padding:** Space between the content and its border.

```css
div {
    margin: 20px;
    padding: 15px;
}
```

## 9. CSS Width and Height

These properties control the dimensions of an element.

```css
div {
    width: 300px;
    height: 150px;
}
```

## 10. CSS Box Model

The CSS box model consists of four parts:

1. Content
2. Padding
3. Border
4. Margin

It determines how space and dimensions are calculated around HTML elements.

## 11. CSS Display Property

The `display` property controls how an element appears in the layout.

```css
div {
    display: block;
}
```

Common values:
- `block` – Starts on a new line and usually takes the available width.
- `inline` – Stays within the same line.
- `inline-block` – Stays inline while allowing width and height.
- `flex` – Creates a flexible layout.
- `grid` – Creates a grid layout.
- `none` – Hides the element and removes it from the layout.

## 12. CSS Hover Effect

The `:hover` pseudo-class applies styles when the mouse pointer is over an element.

```css
button {
    background-color: blue;
    color: white;
}

button:hover {
    background-color: green;
}
```

## 13. CSS Flexbox

Flexbox is used to arrange elements in a row or column.

```css
.container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
}
```

- `justify-content` – Aligns items along the main axis.
- `align-items` – Aligns items along the cross axis.
- `gap` – Adds space between items.

## 14. CSS Comments

Comments explain code and are ignored by the browser.

```css
/* This is a CSS comment */
h1 {
    color: red;
}
```

## 15. Simple CSS Program

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>CSS Example</title>
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: lightyellow;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
        }

        h1 {
            color: blue;
            font-size: 35px;
        }

        p {
            color: green;
            font-size: 20px;
        }

        button {
            background-color: blue;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }

        button:hover {
            background-color: green;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to CSS</h1>
    <p>This is my first CSS program.</p>
    <button>Click Me</button>
</body>
</html>
```

## Conclusion

CSS is an important technology used to design attractive and responsive webpages. By learning CSS selectors, colors, fonts, borders, spacing, layouts, and hover effects, we can create well-designed websites.
